+# Fixed continuation budget and literature basis
+
+30 September 2026. Proposed, unexecuted. User's “proceed” authorizes the next twice-reviewed convergence experiment and related primary-paper investigation. Bounded native extension of existing full-subset controls; preserve branch, user proposal changes and all review/evidence records. The additional budget is a fixed local diagnostic choice, not a number prescribed by the literature.
+
+## Why this question
+
+At update2000 the three saved Adam proposals still lower fitting force error slightly. Force-only and balanced source force losses declined over1500→2000, so current evidence does not establish convergence or insufficient capacity. Negative reference-direction slopes did not reliably predict benefit at the two finite distances. Hold model/optimizer/LR/weights/data fixed and extend the training budget before changing several factors at once. Compare all three existing controls, rather than selecting force-only as the preferred model. This is a training-budget sensitivity check, not a proof of optimizer convergence or a competitive model benchmark.
+
+Related primary work: PaiNN §5 reports a validation-driven LR schedule and larger representations (https://proceedings.mlr.press/v139/schutt21a.html), unlike our fixed-LR16feature fitting-only diagnostic. Landscape17 evaluates organization of the PES beyond point errors (https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.16425). eSEN and Bigi examine physical-task/smoothness/consistency failures (https://proceedings.mlr.press/v267/fu25h.html; https://proceedings.mlr.press/v267/bigi25a.html). None certifies that4000additional updates suffice here. Separate literature evidence, local observations and untested inferences in the paper notes. Latest Bigi2026 large-data results provide counterevidence to blanket claims against unconstrained models (https://arxiv.org/abs/2601.16195).
+
+## Immutable source and controls
+
+Exactly replay→balanced→force-only, each loaded from its historical final2000update/count checkpoint with actual saved moments, model parameters and unchanged normalization. Reuse optimizer_preflight through strict copied diagnostic controls: complete100raw+2compact pins and all historical source configurations, arrays/memberships, baselines, predictions and counters before fitting. Additionally pin all18optimizer-diagnostic outputs plus its compact report (118raw+3compact total), enforce its complete verified36cell/72step/18probe matrix, raw/compact summary/observation identity and state hashes; verify these new control JSON records before the parent prepared-array loader. All source files and source state hashes rechecked after each arm/end. Original source checkpoints never written.
+
+Same128fitting/16fully-fittedanchor, seed0, float64CPU, zero-head16features/degree1/2iterations/8basis/5Å model, train-only scales, LR.001, exact saved weights. Baseline coverage/loss trainers stay unchanged. Generic training resume remains disabled; this new isolated continuation explicitly uses immutable original raw baselines and saved optimizer counters, with no validation selection state or new training data. New run root is protected, no overwrite/retry/adaptive extension.
+
+## Budget and scoring
+
+Each arm commits exactly4000additional full-subset updates, from global2000 to6000; incoming state/count2000, outgoing6000. Sequential16frame microbatches at fixed incoming parameters, one Adam update after128frames. Additional committed training exposures512000perarm, cumulative768000 including source256000; discarded compilation/warmup128perarm counted separately. Warmup proposal discarded, verify original incoming state hashes unchanged. Call existing weighted step builder; no new optimizer/weight/LR/schedule/head/capacity/seed/GPU. A finite nonzero derivative is not a convergence certificate.
+
+Evaluate at source2000, first2001 (reconcile against prior stateful scale1 probe on both raw objectives/roles at1e-10/1e-8), and every100updates2100…6000: exactly42observations if complete. Raw/per-group/equal-group/overlap metrics, immutable original energy/force fractions and weighted losses; never rebase to update2000 errors or recenter energy. Original strict joint gate<.1 on fitting AND anchor; force-only force acceptance separate, cannot clear joint/fullpilot. No early stop on learning success, best checkpoint selection or heldout access. Record every schedule point, sign of finite changes and final stop reason.
+
+Descriptive terminal-window change for each raw objective/role: (MSE5500−MSE6000)/MSE5500. Report signed value; absolute relative change<.01 receives only “small terminal-window change”, not converged/stationary/capacity-limited. Always report raw endpoints and earlier trend, and declare unavailable if window incomplete or denominatorzero. This classification cannot change learning acceptance or authorize an intervention.
+
+Per-arm1200s cap includes preparation/compilation/warmup/updates/scoring/checkpoint/subprocess verification; controller3900s cap includes preflight/outputs. Boundary checks with reserved output/probe time, no forced cancellation of active JAX operations; cap overrun invalidates execution, partial work preserved and later arms blocked. Save synchronized completed/attempted update counts separately; interrupted update unknown partial work, do not invent committed exposures. Save last verified state/history on failure, no automatic research retry. Fresh-process exhaustive saved-input predictions after each completed arm, raw<1e-10 absolute tolerance, count/update6000, exact normalization and final state-hash checks inside the same fresh subprocess; receipt binds verification to exact checkpoint SHA256. Prediction-preserving counter/normalization corruption must fail. State/provenance/source hashes and both original gates verified.
+
+## Failure and interpretation
+
+Preflight, bad numeric/control settings, hash/array/metadata/count/reference, nonfinite, first-step mismatch, wall or fresh-process failure invalidates execution/blocks later arms. Every arm has prospective and immediate outcome evidence with source identities/settings/gates/limits, last completed global/local count, partial histories/checkpoint and hashes. Report derives actual exposures/counts from records; incomplete continuation is not a completed6000budget. Missing42observations/probe/counter/source verification cannot pass reporting interpretation. Atomic JSON and versioned atomic checkpoint persistence retain earlier verified history/state if new writes fail. Handle KeyboardInterrupt explicitly, including during unsynchronized updates; record independent controller failure evidence if arm final persistence fails. Persisted snapshot counts and in-memory synchronized counts remain distinct when writes fail. All failures retained.
+
+Improvement with extra budget supports budget sensitivity in this fixed setting. Failure after6000 does not prove capacity limitation, a bad optimizer, eventual impossibility, or convergence; one seed and fully fitted anchor. Passing fitting gates motivates separately reviewed pilot work, not automatic heldout evaluation. No direct-force/consistency model training or physical geometry-relaxation task yet.
+
+## Implementation and completion
+
+Create isolated convergence_runs.py/controller; extend CLI diagnose-convergence-budget. Tests: saved moment continuation versus uninterrupted tiny-model reference, no resets, immutable baseline/inputs/source states, first-step oracle, exact counts/history/warmup, strict prereq/config gates before arrays, source corruption, new-process counters, wall/partial/block/exception handling. JSON-only report with completeness guards, terminal-window arithmetic and physical/optimizer limitations. Full193prior+new tests before one exact production invocation at committed code. Inspect figures; append all numerical/literature findings. Two independent scientific/engineering reviews before product implementation, re-review material amendments; native work only. Fresh final independent review where available, author-verified fixes, no research rerun; Obsidian CLI backup/readback, durable archive/local commits, preserve all records.
