+E.2. Training Time Analysis
+Table A10 provides training times measured for experiments with and without PIWSL. The training time is measured for
+a single training epoch and is averaged over five epochs in total. The experiments were performed using 1000 training
+configurations from the ANI-1x data set. We used a mini-batch of six. The table indicates that PIWSL increases the training
+time by a factor of two to three compared to the baseline (due to the additional gradient calculations). This is primarily
+because our PITC and PISC losses effectively double or triple the number of data labels, resulting in a proportional increase
+in training time due to the expanded set of training labels. This issue can be mitigated by employing the 2pt-PISC loss
+introduced in section E.3.2, which eliminates the need to estimate the third conformation. Table A11 presents the average
+training times per epoch for MACE-OFF over ten epochs, as discussed in subsection 5.4. These results indicate that even the
+MACE-OFF (large) model requires less than twice the training time while achieving approximately a 40% reduction in error.
+We emphasize that the PIWSL approach only alters training time; the inference time is unaffected.
